      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add conversation identity modes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCloses #98542.\n\nOpenClaw had the routing and sender facts needed to distinguish personal, explicitly bound service-agent, and external/shared conversations, but no single closed decision prevented unresolved audiences from inheriting a personal agent identity and workspace.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Adds one canonical personal / organization-team / external-shared identity decision.\n- Enforces the decision before personal session context, provider hydration, workspace instructions, or agent execution.\n- Reuses existing bindings, route provenance, sender ownership, pairing stores, channel allowlists, and per-sender policy; no new public RBAC/config surface.\n- Preserves pairing as the route to stable direct-message ownership, including carrying the effective pairing-store allowlist through the final identity recheck.\n- Covers core routing plus channel/plugin ingress, voice/session paths, tests, and documentation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOwner direct messages may use the personal identity. Team/organization mode requires an explicit non-default service-agent binding. Unbound guests and unresolved shared audiences fail closed before personal context loads.\n\nThis is intentionally a draft. It is pinned to the last clean foundation floor (`1e20f15581f9fe9132768379bd80cc74c047b8cc`) because rebasing the broad stack onto current `main` produces extensive overlapping conflicts; it needs owner-guided sequencing and a later conflict-resolution rebase.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Fresh autoreview found and drove fixes for pairing ordering, pairing-store ownership propagation, provider-qualified owners, unsafe IRC nickname admission, and IPv6 hostmasks; final exact patch clean with no actionable findings (0.90 confidence).\n- Final focused local fallback: Feishu 92/92, Line 45/45, IRC 9/9, Zalo/Zalo Personal 29/29, plus a final Zalo command-authorization regression run 3/3.\n- Testbox `tbx_01kwp34a452xp6gyegssrq2d3a` / Actions 28700219768 — SMS 4/4 plus extension production/test types passed.\n- Prior focused matrices covered voice restore (13 tests) and identity/channel suites (197, 251, 243, 157, 51, and 42 tests).\n- Fresh Testbox reruns were unavailable because leases repeatedly shut down during checkout/hydration. Narrow local fallback covers the final repair; GitHub CI is the fresh exact-head broad gate.\n\n## Dependencies and Sequencing\n\n- Builds on the prepared conversation capability/profile foundation from #98536 (`ab2f6...`).\n- Review/land the foundation first; then rebase and resolve this draft against current `main`; then require exact-head CI and owner review.\n- Non-goals: broad RBAC, credential/egress policy, new memory namespaces, UI, version/release work.\n",
        "branch": "codex/conversation-identity-modes",
